{
  "_comment": [
    "DEV-ONLY: every setting gxwid reads from the registry, set to what the dev",
    "VM wants. gxwi.regman says what each one means.",
    "",
    "dev/run-gxwid.sh applies this each time it starts gxwid, so a change here",
    "takes a dev/push.sh to reach a running VM.",
    "",
    "A key is made only if its parent is there, so every one on the way is",
    "listed. The keys inherit the hive's descriptor: SYSTEM and Administrators",
    "in full, Authenticated Users to read. That is what Compositor needs, since",
    "whoever can write it chooses what runs as everyone who logs on.",
    "",
    "Listen is every address because the host reaches the guest through QEMU's",
    "forward. Compositor is where dev/run-gxwid.sh puts a copy of whichever",
    "compositor is on the share.",
    "",
    "OverlaySession and OverlayUsername are not here, so the dev VM has no",
    "overlay. dev/browser/overlay.mjs sets and removes them with `reg` while",
    "gxwid runs, which is the point of them: they apply live."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Software" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Software\\GXWI",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Listen", "type": "sz", "data": "0.0.0.0:7780" },
        { "name": "Compositor", "type": "sz", "data": "/tmp/gxwi-compositor" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Software\\GXWI\\Logon",
      "values": [
        { "name": "Name", "type": "sz", "data": "GXWI dev VM" },
        { "name": "Notice", "type": "multi", "data": [
          "This is a development machine. Anything on it may be gone at the next boot.",
          "Log on as alice (alice-dev-password), or as peios with no password."
        ] }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
